Found by a coordinator feature-gap review, 2026-08-30. Depends on B035.

## Gap
Three diagnostic families whose fix is a rename or a const adjustment. These
are last in the quick-fix sequence because each offers TWO valid alternatives
and none can be auto-applied.

- `VariableShadow` ("Variable 'x' hides another variable of same name in outer
  scope") — fix: rename the inner declaration. The rename machinery already
  exists (`rename_provider` is live, `src/server/mod.rs:1416`), so the action
  should reuse it rather than hand-rolling an edit. Suggested name generation
  must avoid colliding with anything else in scope.
- `DuplicateFunction` ("A function with the same name and parameters already
  exists", ERROR, compile aborts) — fix: rename one of the two. Which one is
  the user's call, so offer the rename on the diagnosed declaration only.
- `NonConstMethodOnConstReceiver { method, object_type }` — the game fails
  with "No matching signatures to 'T::M() const'". TWO fixes, both legitimate:
  (a) mark the METHOD `const` at its declaration (cross-file edit, correct
  when the method genuinely does not mutate); (b) drop `const` from the
  RECEIVER's type (local edit, correct when the caller should not have
  promised constness). Offer both, prefer neither.

## Design decision (coordinator, 2026-08-30)
None of these are `isPreferred` and none participate in
`source.fixAll.openplanet`. Every one of them either changes an API surface or
picks between two intents the tool cannot distinguish. Offering them on
right-click is right; applying them on save is not.

For `NonConstMethodOnConstReceiver` fix (a): the rule is deliberately scoped to
workspace-local classes because external typedb methods carry no const flag
(see the variant's doc comment in checker.rs). The fix inherits that scope —
never offer to edit a declaration outside the workspace.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red, one per family.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):

`VariableShadow`:
- local shadowing a local, a parameter, a class field, and a global
- suggested name does not collide with anything in either scope (assert
  against a fixture that already contains the obvious candidate name)
- rename updates ALL references to the inner variable and NONE to the outer
  (this is the whole risk of the fix — test it hard)
- shadow inside a nested block, inside a loop body, inside a lambda if
  supported
- the existing "prefix with underscore" suppression is unaffected

`DuplicateFunction`:
- two top-level functions, same name, same param types -> action on the second
- same name, DIFFERENT param types -> no diagnostic, no action (overloads are
  legal; regression guard)
- namespaced duplicates in the same namespace -> diagnosed and fixable
- same name in DIFFERENT namespaces -> no diagnostic
- rename updates call sites of the renamed declaration only

`NonConstMethodOnConstReceiver`:
- both actions offered, distinct titles, neither preferred
- fix (a) edits the method declaration in ANOTHER file and the edit is a
  proper multi-file `WorkspaceEdit`
- fix (a) NOT offered when the method is external (typedb) — scope guard
- fix (b) edits only the receiver declaration
- a const method called on a const receiver -> no diagnostic (guard)
- a non-const method on a NON-const receiver -> no diagnostic (guard)
- inherited method from a base class -> fix (a) targets the declaring class

